 future that grisha  has seen is absolutely horrifying grisha  begged zeke to try to somehow stop aaron  and all of this tells us that aaron has  some extremely gamer plans that he is  about to set into motion in the near  future after this incident aaron and  zeke find themselves outside of grisha's  memories and back inside the coordinate  aaron actually thanks zeke for taking  him on a tour of grisha's memories  because if he hadn't done that using the  founder then aaron who doesn't have  royal blood would not have been able to  do what he just did four years earlier  when he had touched historia's hand  aaron was able to clearly see many of  grisha's memories in attack on titan it  is not unusual for a titan shifter to  see the memories of a previous shifter  especially if that previous shifter was  directly related to the current shifter  by blood when we couple that with the  fact that aaron possesses the founding  titan it isn't too surprising that after  making direct contact with historia's  royal blood aaron was able to see more  of gracious memories even more clearly  than ever before and on top of grisha's  own memories aaron also saw his future  self within grisha's memories he already  saw this very moment that we just  witnessed with frida and the rhys family  as it happened through grisha's eyes and  he has been waiting for it and planning  for it for the past four years but how  did aaron manage to interfere how was he  able to speak to his father directly and  even influence him in the past i mean  it's one thing for aaron to have  memories of all of this happening but  it's another thing altogether for him to  be able to directly communicate with and  even manipulate his father in the past  did aaron literally travel through time  in order to speak to grisha is aaron  using the founding titan to convey  messages to grisha in the past does  aaron have special ghost powers  well we have to remember that at this  point in the story zeke is the one who  is in control of the founding titan not  aaron this means that the only power  that aaron has at his disposal is the  attack titan power and the attack  titan's special ability is to send the  current user's memories back to the past  aaron interfered in the past only by  sharing his own memories of this  incident with grisha so essentially  while grisha was going through this  event in what was for him the present  time he also at the same time  experienced aaron's memory of aaron and  zeke witnessing the same event within  grisha's memories yes i know this sounds  confusing so let me try to simplify as  grisha is going through the act of  talking to frida he is also seeing the  entire event from aaron's perspective at  the same time and that's because aaron  chose to send those exact memories back  to grisha through the attack titan the  things that aaron and zeke are saying  cannot be heard by anyone other than  grisha and he knows what's being said  only because he has access to aaron's  memories similarly the only reason why  grisha can see zeke as a bearded man in  that moment is because aaron sent him  his own memory of bearded zeke watching  grisha this means that grisha can't  actually see aaron because he's seeing  zeke through aaron's eyes whenever  grisha is seeing future zeke it is  because future aaron is also standing  there and looking at zeke as well that  said grisha does know where exactly  aaron is located at any point in time  because again he's seeing everything  through his own eyes and through aaron's  eyes at the same time in short grisha  can perceive aaron and zeke only because  he can see aaron's point of view as  aaron watched the memory of the exact  same event that grisha is currently  living through grisha is seeing the  event through his own eyes and through  aaron's eyes at the same time but  because grisha is experiencing both  things at once the event as it is  happening and aaron's memories of  watching the event he is able to react  in real time to what zeke and aaron are  doing and saying in the future and as  grisha reacts zeke and aaron see those  reactions as they are watching grisha so  it appears as if they are directly  communicating in real time even though  they are actually nearly a decade apart  the actual event happened nearly a  decade before aaron and zeke decide to  watch grisha's memory of that event and  if you're wondering how aaron was able  to touch grisha's shoulder or how grisha  was able to hug zeke they weren't really  making physical contact it only appeared  that way after all if grisha had hugged  zeke after gaining the founding titan  power then zeke's royal blood would have  activated the founder in that very  moment in reality this was just like two  ghosts hugging each other this was not  real physical contact and yes this does  amount to a predestination paradox also  known as a causality loop if aaron  hadn't sent his memories to grisha  through the attack titan grisha never  would have taken the founding titan from  frieda and given it to aaron and so zeke  and erin never would have been able to  visit grisha's memories in the first  place this is ironic since in a  predestination paradox everything that  happens is destined to happen and cannot  be changed which means that aaron's  actions were never truly free even  though freedom was the single biggest  driving force in his life everything he  did was destined to happen and none of  it could ever be changed or at least  that is the most popular and plausible  interpretation of events a different  interpretation would require getting  into some heavy theoretical speculation  about alternate timelines but that is a  topic for another video subscribe if you  want to see that one big question here  is why would grisha ask zeke to stop  aaron but then still go through with  giving aaron the attack and founding  titan powers we know that aaron was only  selectively sharing his memories with  grisha up to this point he was only  showing grisha what he needed him to see  in order to do exactly what aaron wanted  him to do but after he takes the founder  grisha says that he has seen aaron's  memories from even further into the  future and he says that what aaron is  going to do is absolutely horrible and  has to be stopped and yet after all of  that he still goes through with  transferring the titan powers to aaron  the predestination paradox suggests that  grisha had no way to stop this aaron had  to get the titan powers in order to send  those memories to grisha in the first  place so it was impossible for grisha to  keep the powers from aaron because that  would have created an unresolvable  grandfather paradox maybe grisha tried  to do things differently but the events  that followed led him to the same  inevitable outcome no matter what he  tried maybe he changed his mind about  everything after learning what actually  happened to shiganshina maybe he was  afraid that changing the inevitable  would actually destroy the entire  timeline and everyone in it which would  be even worse than whatever aaron was up  to or maybe grisha was just placing his  faith in the fact that zeke or someone  else could ultimately stop aaron in the  future definitely let me know down in  the comments why you think grisha  decided to still go through with handing  the titan powers over to aaron despite  the fact that he was terrified of what  aaron was planning to do i hope that  this video was useful to you in terms of  explaining all of this time traveling  memories stuff it is not technically  these people traveling through time but  the memories are definitely traveling  through time feel free to let me know  how you feel about this twist down in  the comments below if you're looking for  a video to watch next check out this one  i made recently about all of erin's  different titan forms and powers in  attack on titan from the beginning of  the story until the end the link is in  th